<Mail: vincent.dufour@inria.fr>			

---------------------------------------------------------------- DESCRIPTION -----------------------------------------------

The "mesa_gazebo_replay" sub-folder contains the files allowing you to replay the simulations carried out on MESA
in Gazebo from the "drone-simulator" simulator of the CITI CHROMA team.

---------------------------------------------------------------- CONTENT ---------------------------------------------------

5 files:
- compress_coords.py => takes as input the name of the .json file containing the coordinates generated by MESA
			and reduces the number of steps by removing the points on the same straight line.
			==> creates a new json file entitled "compressed_coords.json".

- modify_logs.py => takes as input the name of the .json file containing the coordinates generated by MESA and offers to
		    perform several transformations (see --options) on the data. 
                    HAS TO BE USED with "--split true" argument if the run_mesa_gazebo_sim.sh is used with its second 
		    argument set as "true".
                    It will create several json file for each drone to publish coordinates in rostopic in parallel which
		    speeds up the simulation and assure "synchronicity" between drones.

- playback_output.json => original file containing the coordinates generated by MESA

- read_coord_v2.cpp => C++ script allowing the reading of the .json file and the publication in the topics
			during the simulation under gazebo.
			To be compiled: $ g ++ -o readjson read_coord_v2.cpp -ljsoncpp
			==> creates a C++ executable name "readjson".

- run_mesa_gazebo_sim.sh => general bash script launching the simulator, spawning the number of drones 
			    at their starting position, running the C++ script to read and post the waypoints. 
			    Start the simulation.


---------------------------------------------------------------- IMPORTANT -------------------------------------------------

There is a modification to be made in a script before launching the run_mesa_gazebo_sim.sh script.

In the script gazebo_interfaces/launch/multi_pilot_traj.launch, the last part of the code is indicated as "To be commented
when used with run_mesa_gazebo_sim.sh". Check if it is actually commented, it avoids issues during launch.



---------------------------------------------------------------- HOW IT WORKS ----------------------------------------------	

When the user receives a .json file containing coordinates from MESA, there are 2 steps to perform:

- run the python script: $ python3 compress_coords.py --file coords_origin.json 
			 => creates a compressed_coords.json file

- run the bash script: $ ./run_mesa_gazebo_sim.sh compressed_coords.json

NB:
Check if the read_coord_v2.cpp has already been compiled (executable "readjson" available), otherwise simulation won't run.




